---
import LegalLayout from "../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { BRAND } from "@vc/config";
import { isMarketingHost } from "../../server/public-blog";
import { publicRuntimeEnv } from "../../server/runtime";
import { isDirectInternalRootHit } from "../../lib/internal-root";

const env = publicRuntimeEnv(Astro);
if (isDirectInternalRootHit(Astro.originPathname, Astro.url.pathname) || env.selfHosted || !isMarketingHost(Astro.request, env)) return new Response("Not found", { status: 404 });
---
<LegalLayout title="About vibecms" description="An open-source CMS built for AI agents and the people who own their work." updated="September 27, 2026">
  <p>
    vibecms is a CMS for developers, indie hackers, and small technical teams who want an AI
    agent to help run a blog, changelog, or notes site. The agent can draft, preview, and publish
    through MCP over HTTPS, a REST API, or the CLI. The person who owns the site stays in charge
    of what goes live. New agent keys are scoped to drafts by default, and publishing access is
    a separate choice made by the owner.
  </p>
  <h2>Control over every change</h2>
  <p>
    Post changes create versions, so the owner can see what changed and restore an earlier
    version. Activity records show the work done in the workspace. A draft can be reviewed in
    preview before the owner approves publication. These controls matter because an agent should
    be useful without taking ownership of a person's writing or publishing decisions.
  </p>
  <h2>Open source and hosting</h2>
  <p>
    The project is <a href={BRAND.repoUrl}>open source</a>. vibecms Cloud runs the hosted
    service; the same repository also supports self-hosting on an operator's own Cloudflare
    D1 and R2 resources. Self-hosting is an option for teams that want to operate their own
    infrastructure, while the hosted service is for people who want a blog without running it.
  </p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    For account, billing, or private questions, email <a href="mailto:support@vibecms.dev">support@vibecms.dev</a>.
    For bugs and feature ideas, open an issue in the public repository. The
    <a href="/legal/support">support page</a> explains what information helps us investigate.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
